#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# barnes_g

#% text
# `barnes_g(z)` gives the Barnes G-function, with `barnes_g(z + 1) = gamma(z)*barnes_g(z)` and `barnes_g(1) = 1`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `G` is entire, with zeros at 0, -1, -2, ... (DLMF 5.17). At positive integers it is the superfactorial: `G(n + 2) = 1!*2!*...*n!`.

#% item
# Positive integers give exact values; machine numbers and balls give numerical values.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
barnes_g(5)
#% output
#= 12

#% cell
barnes_g(1)
#% output
#= 1

#% cell
barnes_g(2.5)
#% output
#= 0.9475739010838258

#% cell
barnes_g(0)
#% output
#= 0

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The functional equation:

#% cell
barnes_g(3.7) - gamma(2.7)*barnes_g(2.7)
#% output
#= 0.0

#% text
# The superfactorial:

#% cell
barnes_g(6) - product(factorial(k), [k, 1, 4])
#% output
#= 0

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `log_barnes_g`, `gamma`, `factorial`
